## Communication Protocols

### Short-Range Protocols (< 100m)

#### **Bluetooth/BLE (Bluetooth Low Energy)**
- **Range**: 10-100 meters
- **Power**: Ultra-low
- **Bandwidth**: 1 Mbps
- **Use Cases**: Wearables, personal devices
- **Frequency**: 2.4 GHz ISM band
- **Latency**: 6-100 ms

#### **Zigbee**
- **Range**: 10-100 meters
- **Power**: Low
- **Bandwidth**: 250 kbps
- **Protocol**: IEEE 802.15.4
- **Use Cases**: Home automation, industrial control
- **Topology**: Mesh network
- **Channels**: 16

#### **NFC (Near Field Communication)**
- **Range**: 4-10 cm
- **Power**: Very low
- **Bandwidth**: 424 kbps
- **Use Cases**: Payment, access control, data transfer
- **Frequency**: 13.56 MHz

#### **Wi-Fi Direct**
- **Range**: 10-100 meters
- **Power**: Moderate
- **Bandwidth**: 54-600 Mbps
- **Use Cases**: File transfer, streaming
- **Advantage**: Direct device-to-device communication

### Medium-Range Protocols (100m - 10km)

#### **Wi-Fi**
- **Range**: 30-100 meters
- **Bandwidth**: 54 Mbps to 1+ Gbps (modern)
- **Power**: Moderate
- **Use Cases**: Homes, offices, public spaces
- **Frequency**: 2.4 GHz / 5 GHz
- **Standard**: IEEE 802.11 a/b/g/n/ac/ax

#### **LoRaWAN (Long Range Wide Area Network)**
- **Range**: 2-10+ km
- **Power**: Very low
- **Bandwidth**: 50 kbps
- **Topology**: Star
- **Use Cases**: Wide-area IoT networks
- **Spreading Factor**: 7-12 (trade-off between speed and range)

#### **Sigfox**
- **Range**: 10-50 km
- **Bandwidth**: 100 bps
- **Power**: Ultra-low
- **Use Cases**: Smart metering, asset tracking
- **Message Size**: 12 bytes max

### Long-Range Protocols (> 10km)

#### **Cellular (4G LTE / 5G)**
- **Range**: 1-50 km
- **Bandwidth**: 10+ Mbps
- **Power**: Moderate to high
- **Use Cases**: Real-time applications, high-bandwidth needs
- **Coverage**: Global

#### **NB-IoT (Narrowband IoT)**
- **Range**: 1-10 km
- **Bandwidth**: 250 kbps
- **Power**: Very low
- **Use Cases**: IoT applications, battery-powered devices
- **Standard**: 3GPP Release 13

#### **LTE-M (LTE for Machines)**
- **Range**: 1-10 km
- **Bandwidth**: 1 Mbps
- **Power**: Low
- **Use Cases**: Moderate-bandwidth IoT applications
- **Latency**: Lower than NB-IoT

