**Feature Engineering for Fault Detection**:
```
VIBRATION FEATURE EXTRACTION:

Time-Domain Features:
├─ RMS (Root Mean Square): √(mean of x²)
│  └─ Indicates overall vibration energy
│  └─ Normal bearing: 2-3 mm/s RMS
│  └─ Damaged bearing: 5-10+ mm/s RMS
│
├─ Peak Value: Maximum absolute acceleration
│  └─ Sudden spikes = bearing spalls
│
├─ Crest Factor: Peak / RMS ratio
│  └─ Normal: 3-4
│  └─ Bearing fault: 8-15 (very impulsive)
│
└─ Kurtosis: Measure of "tailedness"
   └─ Normal distribution: ~3.0
   └─ Bearing fault: 8-20 (spiky/impulsive signals)

Frequency-Domain Features (FFT):
├─ Bearing fault frequencies:
│  ├─ BPFO (Ball Pass Frequency Outer): Outer race fault
│  ├─ BPFI (Ball Pass Frequency Inner): Inner race fault
│  └─ FTF (Fundamental Train Frequency): Cage fault
│
├─ Example: 1800 RPM motor (30 Hz shaft frequency)
│  ├─ BPFO ≈ 3.5 × 30 Hz = 105 Hz and harmonics
│  ├─ BPFI ≈ 5.5 × 30 Hz = 165 Hz and harmonics
│  └─ These peaks appear in FFT spectrum when bearing fails
│
└─ Spectral Energy Distribution:
   ├─ Low frequency (0-100 Hz): Imbalance, misalignment
   ├─ Mid frequency (100-500 Hz): Bearing faults
   └─ High frequency (500+): Surface damage, spalling

Envelope Analysis (Demodulation):
├─ High-pass filter: Remove low frequencies
├─ Hilbert transform: Extract signal envelope
├─ Demodulate: Detect bearing fault signatures more clearly
└─ Result: Fault patterns visible earlier in degradation
```

