**Scenario**: Automated Irrigation Management System

```
SMART IRRIGATION SYSTEM:

Environmental Sensors:
├─ Soil Moisture Sensors (capacitive)
│  ├─ Measure volumetric water content
│  ├─ Depth: 0-30 cm, 30-60 cm (root zone)
│  ├─ Calibration: Field-specific (soil type dependent)
│  └─ Accuracy: ±3-5% volumetric water
│
├─ Soil Matric Potential (Tensiometer)
│  ├─ Measure water availability to plant
│  ├─ Units: kPa (kilopascals)
│  ├─ Optimal range: -10 to -80 kPa
│  └─ Below -100 kPa: Plant stress
│
├─ Weather Station:
│  ├─ Rainfall (tipping bucket gauge)
│  ├─ Temperature (air temperature sensor)
│  ├─ Humidity (relative humidity sensor)
│  ├─ Wind speed (anemometer)
│  └─ Solar radiation (pyranometer)
│
└─ Plant Status Sensors:
   ├─ Leaf wetness (disease prevention)
   ├─ Sap flow sensor (plant water usage)
   └─ Thermal imaging (stress detection)

THEORY: Plant Water Requirement (PWR)

Evapotranspiration (ET):
├─ Water loss from soil surface and plant leaves
├─ Formula: ET = ETo × Kc
│  ├─ ETo: Reference evapotranspiration (climate/weather)
│  ├─ Kc: Crop coefficient (crop type, growth stage)
│  ├─ Example: Corn, flowering stage Kc = 1.1-1.15
│  └─ Result: ET varies 2-8 mm/day depending on season
│
├─ Water Balance Model:
│  ├─ Soil water yesterday: SM(t-1)
│  ├─ Add: Rainfall or irrigation: P(t)
│  ├─ Subtract: Evapotranspiration: ET(t)
│  ├─ Result: Soil water today: SM(t) = SM(t-1) + P(t) - ET(t)
│  └─ Goal: Keep SM between field capacity and wilting point
│
└─ Irrigation Scheduling:
   ├─ If SM drops below threshold (e.g., -50 kPa):
   ├─ Calculate irrigation need: Depletion = ETc × days_since_rain
   ├─ Account for irrigation efficiency (0.75-0.95)
   ├─ Calculate volume: Volume = Depletion / Efficiency
   ├─ Schedule irrigation to fill soil back to field capacity
   └─ Minimize deep percolation (water loss below root zone)

SYSTEM BENEFITS:
├─ Water savings: 20-40% reduction
├─ Yield improvement: 10-30% increase
├─ Energy savings: Pumping only when needed
├─ Labor reduction: Automated scheduling
└─ Environmental: Reduced nitrate leaching
```

**Decision Support Algorithm**:
```
IRRIGATION DECISION MODEL:

Real-time Inputs (hourly):
├─ Soil moisture: 75% field capacity
├─ Weather forecast: No rain next 3 days
├─ ET rate: 5 mm/day (current conditions)
├─ Crop coefficient: 0.95 (current growth stage)
└─ Root depth: 600 mm

Calculation:
1. Available water capacity (AWC):
   ├─ Field capacity (FC): 30% by volume
   ├─ Wilting point (WP): 15% by volume
   ├─ AWC = FC - WP = 15%
   ├─ For 600 mm root depth: 600 × 0.15 = 90 mm available
   └─ Currently depleted: 25% of capacity = 22.5 mm used

2. Forecasted depletion (next 3 days):
   ├─ Daily ET = 5 mm × 0.95 = 4.75 mm/day
   ├─ 3-day total: 4.75 × 3 = 14.25 mm
   ├─ Available remaining: 22.5 + (90 - 22.5) = 90 mm
   ├─ Safety margin: Irrigate when 70% depleted
   ├─ Depletion threshold: 90 × 0.7 = 63 mm
   └─ Current + Forecasted = 22.5 + 14.25 = 36.75 mm < 63 mm
      → NO IRRIGATION NEEDED YET

3. Irrigation application (if triggered):
   ├─ Goal: Bring soil back to 50% depletion
   ├─ Target soil moisture: 90 - (90 × 0.5) = 45 mm depleted
   ├─ Irrigation needed: 63 - 45 = 18 mm gross application
   ├─ Accounting for efficiency (0.85): 18 / 0.85 = 21.2 mm applied
   ├─ For center pivot (10 ha): 212,000 liters
   ├─ Pumping time (50 gpm): ~1.4 hours
   └─ Schedule: Start 6 PM (avoid heat, mid-night finish)

4. Weather-based adjustment:
   ├─ 30% chance rain tomorrow (5 mm expected)
   ├─ Updated depletion: 36.75 - 5 = 31.75 mm
   ├─ Below threshold, delay irrigation 24 hours
   └─ Re-evaluate with updated forecast

SYSTEM PERFORMANCE:
├─ Water efficiency: 92-95% (vs 70-75% manual)
├─ Labor hours: 200 hours/season → 10 hours/season
├─ Fuel costs: $1,500 reduced to $400/season
├─ Yield variance: Reduced 20% (more consistent)
└─ Environmental: Nitrate leaching reduced 25-35%
