## Interview Concepts & Q&A

### 1. Protocol Selection & Trade-offs

#### **Q: How do you choose between MQTT and HTTP for IoT communication?**

**Answer**: Consider these factors:

| Aspect | MQTT | HTTP |
|--------|------|------|
| **Connection Model** | Persistent (stateful) | Stateless (request-response) |
| **Bandwidth** | Low (header: 2 bytes minimum) | High (header: larger overhead) |
| **Latency** | Very low (persistent connection) | Higher (handshake per request) |
| **Power Consumption** | Low (always-on connection) | Higher (repeated connections) |
| **QoS Options** | 3 levels (0, 1, 2) | None (HTTP doesn't guarantee) |
| **Publish/Subscribe** | Native support | Requires polling |
| **Complexity** | Medium | Low |
| **Use Case** | Battery devices, streaming | Web integration, REST APIs |

**Practical Example**:
```
Smart Home Sensor (Battery-powered):
├─ MQTT: ✓ Ideal
├─ Publishes: "home/kitchen/temp" = 22.5
├─ Consumes: 5mW average
├─ Battery life: 2+ years
└─ Connection established once, stays open

Weather Dashboard (Cloud service):
├─ HTTP: ✓ Better
├─ Request: GET /api/weather
├─ No persistent connection needed
├─ Easier REST API integration
└─ Simpler infrastructure scaling
```

#### **Q: What's the difference between Zigbee and LoRaWAN?**

**Answer**:
```
ZIGBEE (IEEE 802.15.4):
├─ Range: 10-100 meters
├─ Bandwidth: 250 kbps
├─ Power: Low (AAA batteries, 1-2 years)
├─ Mesh networking: Yes (devices relay messages)
├─ Coverage model: Indoor/Local networks
├─ Topology: Fully configurable (mesh, star)
├─ Latency: 10-100 ms
├─ Use case: Home automation, building control
│
└─ Example: Philips Hue lights network
   ├─ Bridge gateway
   ├─ Lights discover each other
   ├─ Automatic mesh formation
   └─ One light can control another's signal strength

LORAWAN (Long Range Wide Area):
├─ Range: 2-10+ km (line-of-sight)
├─ Bandwidth: 50 kbps
├─ Power: Ultra-low (10+ years battery)
├─ Mesh networking: No (star topology only)
├─ Coverage model: City/Wide area
├─ Gateway capacity: 10,000+ devices per gateway
├─ Latency: 100ms-several seconds
├─ Use case: Wide area IoT networks, smart cities
│
└─ Example: Smart meter network
   ├─ Meters send once per hour
   ├─ Single gateway covers 10 km radius
   ├─ Battery lasts 10 years (minimal transmissions)
   └─ Central server processes all data
```

**Decision Tree**:
```
"Range needed < 100m?"
├─ YES → Zigbee / BLE
├─ NO → "Coverage area < 10 km?"
│       ├─ YES → LoRaWAN / Sigfox
│       └─ NO → Cellular (4G/5G)
│
"Power critical?"
├─ YES (battery > 5 years) → LoRaWAN
├─ NO → Zigbee or WiFi
```

