## Interview Questions & Answers

### **Basic IoT Concepts**

#### **Q1: What is the main difference between IoT, M2M, and IIoT?**

**Expected Answer:**
```
IoT (Internet of Things):
├─ Broad category: Any internet-connected device
├─ Scope: Consumer devices, smart homes, wearables
├─ Examples: Smart phone, fitness tracker, smart thermostat
└─ Focus: Data collection & consumer convenience

M2M (Machine-to-Machine):
├─ Devices communicate directly (no human involved)
├─ Scope: Specific automated communication
├─ Examples: Vending machine → billing system
└─ Focus: Automation between machines

IIoT (Industrial IoT):
├─ Specialized IoT for industries
├─ Scope: Manufacturing, energy, logistics
├─ Examples: Factory sensors, oil rig monitoring
└─ Focus: Productivity, safety, cost reduction

KEY DIFFERENCES:
IoT: Consumer-focused, varied use cases, less rigorous
M2M: Point-to-point communication, specific automation
IIoT: Industrial standards, reliability critical, 99.99% uptime

EXAMPLE:
├─ Consumer IoT: Your smart home device
├─ M2M: Device auto-orders supplies when stock low
└─ IIoT: Factory equipment predicts maintenance need
```

