### **System Design Questions**

#### **Q11: Design a real-time fleet tracking system for 5000 vehicles**

**Expected Answer:**
```
REQUIREMENTS:
├─ 5,000 vehicles sending GPS location
├─ Update frequency: Every 10 seconds
├─ Requirement: Real-time position on map
├─ Dashboard: Show all vehicles live
├─ Storage: Track history (1 year)
├─ Analytics: Route optimization, fuel efficiency
└─ Throughput: 5,000 devices × 6 updates/min = 500 updates/sec

ARCHITECTURE:

LAYER 1: DEVICE (Vehicle GPS Unit)
├─ GPS module: Gets latitude/longitude
├─ Cellular: 4G/LTE (good coverage for vehicles)
├─ Message: {device_id, lat, lng, speed, timestamp}
├─ Size: ~50 bytes
├─ Frequency: Every 10 seconds
└─ Protocol: MQTT (persistent connection, real-time)

LAYER 2: INGESTION (Gateway/Broker)
├─ MQTT broker: 5,000 concurrent connections
├─ Single broker capacity: 10,000 connections
├─ Need: 1 broker sufficient (but add 1 backup)
├─ Total throughput: 500 msg/sec
├─ Broker load: 20% (plenty of capacity)
└─ Cost: $2,000/month for cloud broker

LAYER 3: PROCESSING (Stream)
├─ Real-time stream processor
├─ Tool: Kafka Streams or Apache Flink
├─ Operations:
│  ├─ Validate: Check lat/lng in valid range
│  ├─ Enrich: Add vehicle name, driver from DB
│  ├─ Calculate: Distance traveled, speed
│  ├─ Detect: Overspeeding (speed > 120 km/h)
│  └─ Filter: Only store every 10th update to DB (reduce DB load)
│
├─ Output:
│  ├─ Latest position → Cache (Redis)
│  ├─ Alerts → Notification service
│  └─ Historical data → Time-series database
│
└─ Latency: < 500ms (acceptable for vehicles)

LAYER 4: STORAGE

Cache (Redis):
├─ Latest position of all 5,000 vehicles
├─ Expires: 15 seconds (should have update by then)
├─ Size: 5,000 vehicles × 100 bytes = 500KB
├─ Read: 1 request/sec per user (fast, from cache)
├─ Cost: Tiny ($10-50/month)
└─ Benefit: Sub-millisecond response times

Time-Series Database (InfluxDB):
├─ Historical location data
├─ Store: Every 10th update (reduce load)
├─ Frequency: 50 updates/sec (vs 500)
├─ Retention: 1 year
├─ Size: 50 updates/sec × 50 bytes × 31M sec/year = 77TB
├─ Compression: 10x compression → 7.7TB actual
├─ Cost: $500-2,000/month
└─ Queries: Analytics, history playback

LAYER 5: ANALYTICS

Batch Processing:
├─ Daily job: Analyze all vehicles
├─ Metrics: Distance driven, fuel used, idle time
├─ Output: Reports (CSV, dashboard)
├─ Frequency: Once/day (overnight)
└─ Cost: Low ($100/month, off-peak compute)

Machine Learning:
├─ Model: Predict vehicle maintenance needs
├─ Input: Mileage, acceleration patterns, engine diagnostics
├─ Output: "Maintenance needed in 1000 miles"
├─ Benefit: Reduce breakdowns
└─ Cost: $500/month (model serving)

LAYER 6: PRESENTATION (User Interface)

Web Dashboard:
├─ Real-time map with 5,000 vehicle icons
├─ Click vehicle: See last 10 locations
├─ Features:
│  ├─ Filter by route, driver, status
│  ├─ Show geofences (delivery zones)
│  ├─ Alert: Vehicle overspeeding
│  └─ Analytics: Fleet efficiency
│
├─ Frontend: React/Vue.js
├─ Updates: WebSocket (real-time)
├─ Performance: 100ms refresh (smooth)
└─ Cost: $200/month (static hosting)

Mobile App:
├─ Driver's phone shows personal vehicle
├─ Dispatch: See all assigned vehicles
├─ Manager: See all fleet
├─ Push notifications: Alerts, instructions
└─ Cost: $200/month app hosting

COMPLETE SYSTEM:

┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ 5,000 Vehicles (GPS Units)               │
│ Sending every 10 sec                     │
└────────┬─────────────────────────────────┘
         │ 4G/LTE (MQTT)
┌────────▼─────────────────────────────────┐
│ MQTT Broker (Cloud)                      │
