### **Troubleshooting & Operations Questions**

#### **Q12: Describe your troubleshooting approach for a deployed IoT system**

**Expected Answer:**
```
PROBLEM: "Devices are not sending data for 30 minutes"

STEP 1: IDENTIFY SCOPE & SEVERITY (5 minutes)
├─ How many devices affected?
│  ├─ All 5,000? → Critical (all users impacted)
│  ├─ 500? → Major (some regions down)
│  └─ 5? → Minor (isolated issue)
│
├─ How long down?
│  ├─ 30 min → Revenue impact
│  ├─ Ask: Are customers aware? Yes/No
│  └─ Decision: Page on-call engineer? YES
│
├─ Which devices? (same type/location/version?)
│  └─ Example: "All GPS units in NYC, firmware v1.5"
│
└─ Communication: Alert status page
   └─ "We're investigating data delays"

STEP 2: CHECK INFRASTRUCTURE (10 minutes)

Broker Health:
├─ Broker up? Check dashboard
├─ Broker CPU: < 50%? Yes/No
├─ Broker memory: < 80%? Yes/No
├─ Broker connections: 5,000 active? Check
├─ Broker error logs: Any critical errors?
│
└─ Test: Send test message to broker
   └─ Success? Yes/No

Database Health:
├─ Primary DB up? Check heartbeat
├─ Read latency: Normal (< 100ms)?
├─ Write latency: Normal (< 500ms)?
├─ Disk space: > 10% free?
├─ Error logs: Any OOM (out of memory)?
│
└─ Test: Query latest temperature
   └─ Returns data? Yes/No

Processor Health:
├─ Stream processor running? Check
├─ CPU: High (> 80%)? Yes/No
├─ Memory: Leaking (increasing)? Yes/No
├─ Lag: Messages queued? Check offset
├─ Error logs: Exceptions/crashes?
│
└─ Test: Check for stuck messages
   └─ Messages older than 10 min? Alert!

STEP 3: CHECK NETWORK LAYER (5 minutes)

Carrier Status:
├─ Cellular provider outage?
│  └─ Check carrier status page
│  └─ Check customer reports
│
├─ Regional connectivity?
│  └─ "All devices in NYC down"
│  └─ Carrier issue likely

Internet Connectivity:
├─ Cloud uptime status: All green?
├─ Network latency: Normal?
├─ Packet loss: < 0.1%?
└─ Test: Ping cloud from edge gateway

STEP 4: CHECK DEVICE LAYER (10 minutes)

Sample Devices:
├─ Pick 3-5 devices from affected group
├─ SSH to device: Can you connect?
├─ Check logs: Any errors since 30 min ago?
├─ Check connectivity: Is WiFi/cellular connected?
├─ Check time sync: Is device time correct?
│
│ Example device logs:
│ ├─ 14:00 "Connected to broker"
│ ├─ 14:05 "Temperature: 22.5"
│ ├─ 14:15 "Connection timeout!"
│ └─ 14:20 "Retry failed, will retry in 5 min"
│
└─ Hypothesis: Devices having connection issues

STEP 5: CHECK APPLICATION LAYER (5 minutes)

API Health:
├─ Dashboard still loading?
├─ API response time: Normal?
├─ API error rate: Elevated?
│
└─ Test: Manual API call
   └─ GET /api/latest-readings
   └─ Returns data? Yes/No

Dashboard:
├─ Showing old data? (stale from cache)
├─ Showing error page? (UI issue)
├─ Showing nothing? (no data reaching frontend)
│
└─ Check:
   └─ Browser console: JavaScript errors?

STEP 6: DETERMINE ROOT CAUSE

Hypothesis 1: Broker Overloaded
├─ Signs: High CPU, high memory, high lag
├─ Action:
│  ├─ Add more brokers (scale up)
│  └─ Check for connection leak
└─ Mitigation: Immediate (< 5 min)

Hypothesis 2: Database Overloaded
├─ Signs: Slow writes, high latency
├─ Action:
│  ├─ Add read replicas
│  ├─ Check for slow queries
│  └─ Check for lock contention
└─ Mitigation: Immediate (< 10 min)

Hypothesis 3: Network Issue
├─ Signs: Devices can't connect, high packet loss
├─ Action:
│  ├─ Contact carrier
│  ├─ Check DNS resolution
│  └─ Check firewall rules
└─ Mitigation: Depends on carrier (5-30 min)

Hypothesis 4: Device Firmware Issue
├─ Signs: All devices same version can't connect
├─ Action:
│  ├─ Restart devices
│  ├─ Factory reset affected units
│  └─ Prepare rollback firmware
└─ Mitigation: Gradual (30-60 min)

Hypothesis 5: Configuration Change
├─ Signs: Issue started right after deployment
├─ Action:
│  ├─ Check recent deployments (in past hour)
│  ├─ Rollback if necessary
│  └─ Identify bad config
└─ Mitigation: Immediate (< 5 min rollback)

STEP 7: RESOLUTION

Example: Root Cause = Broker CPU 100%
├─ Immediate: Add 2 more broker instances
├─ Load balancer: Rebalance traffic
├─ Verify: Data flow resumed
├─ Update status: "Issue resolved at 15:45"
│
├─ Longer term:
│  ├─ Investigate: Why did load spike?
│  ├─ Solution: Auto-scale triggers
│  └─ Testing: Load test to verify

STEP 8: POST-INCIDENT (Next day)

Retrospective:
├─ Timeline:
│  ├─ 14:15 - Issue started
│  ├─ 14:30 - Customer reports
│  ├─ 14:35 - Engineer paged
│  ├─ 14:45 - Root cause identified (CPU maxed)
│  ├─ 14:50 - Resolved (added brokers)
│  └─ 30 min total duration
│
├─ Root cause: Auto-scaling not configured
│
├─ Actions:
│  ├─ Enable auto-scaling for brokers
│  ├─ Add monitoring for broker CPU
│  ├─ Test: Simulate 2x load to verify
│  └─ Deadline: Complete by Friday
│
└─ Communication: Email to team
   └─ "What happened, why, and what we fixed"

TOOLS NEEDED:
├─ Dashboard: Broker metrics (CPU, memory, connections)
├─ Logs: Application logs (errors, warnings)
├─ Testing: Can manually connect to broker
├─ SSH: Can access devices remotely
├─ Monitoring: Alerting on key metrics
└─ Documentation: Architecture diagrams, runbooks
```

